#: src/reference/guide/scope-basics.md:13
msgid "The whole story about keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/guide/scope-basics.md:15
msgid ""
"[Previously](build-definition-basics.md) we pretended that a key like `name` "
"corresponded to one entry in sbt's map of key-value pairs. This was a "
"simplification. In the real builds, each key can have an associated value in "
"more than one context, called a _scope._"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/guide/scope-basics.md:20
msgid "Some concrete examples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/guide/scope-basics.md:22
msgid ""
"if you have multiple subprojects in your build definition, a key can have a "
"different value in each project."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/guide/scope-basics.md:24
msgid ""
"the `compile` key may have a different value for your main sources and your "
"test sources, if you want to compile them differently."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/guide/scope-basics.md:26
msgid ""
"the `scalacOptions` key (which contains Scala compiler options) may have "
"different values when compiling class files (`compile`) or running the REPL "
"(`console`)."
msgstr ""

